title: Pre-Scorecard Sweep — M-09 acceptance-gate precondition (F-25 AC)
purpose: Two gates that must be clean before the scorecard rerun is valid — (a) a C-42 shell-injection sweep across every execSync/execFileSync call site, and (b) a correctness/security code-review of the files changed in this initiative's waves 8-10. The AC requires ZERO outstanding blocking findings.
sweptAt: 2026-07-04T00:00:00Z
sweptBy: w10-p25 (implementer-agent)
diffBase: plan-exec-wave-8-pre
totalBlocking: 0
acGate: PASS — zero blocking findings outstanding

security:
  scope: C-42 injection sweep — every execSync/execFileSync call site in scripts/ hooks/ lib/ inspected for unsanitized interpolation of external/user/dynamic input into a shell string.
  method: grep enumeration of execSync/execFileSync call sites, then read each dynamic (non-literal-first-arg) site and trace the provenance of every interpolated value.
  execCallSitesTotal: 50
  execCallSitesProduction: 35
  execCallSitesTest: 15
  dynamicShellStringSites: 2
  shcInterpolationSites: 1
  historicalD02Note: The two D-02 shell-injection sites (loom-health.ts and loom-version-slot.ts) were already remediated by F-04 — both now call execFileSync with an argv array (loom-health.ts:56, loom-version-slot.ts:65). Verified still argv-based; no shell string.
  findings[3]{id,site,class,provenance,severity,blocking,verdict}:
    SEC-01,scripts/loom-cso.ts:66 execSync(cmd),shell-string-var,cmd is only ever the literal "bun audit --json" or "npm audit --json --audit-level=moderate" (tryRun callers L173/L191); no dynamic input,info,false,safe
    SEC-02,scripts/loom-worktree-scan.ts:71 execSync(cmd),shell-string-var,sh(cmd) receives hardcoded literals plus `git rev-parse --verify --quiet ${cand}` and `git diff --name-only ${base}...HEAD` where cand/base come only from the hardcoded array ["main" "master" "origin/main" "origin/master"] via baseBranch(); no attacker-influenced value reaches the shell,info,false,safe
    SEC-03,scripts/lib/doctor/checks/runner-resolution.ts:41 execFileSync("sh" ["-c" `command -v ${runtime}`]),sh-c-interpolation,runtime is typed "bun" | "node" and defaultProbe is only invoked with those two literals; no dynamic value,info,false,safe
  argvSitesNote: All other production execFileSync sites (git/gh/tar/bunx/npx/tsx invocations) pass arguments as argv arrays with no shell, so repo-derived values (branch names, refs, paths) are never shell-parsed.
  blockingCount: 0

codeReview:
  scope: Correctness + security review of code files changed in waves 8-10 (git diff plan-exec-wave-8-pre..HEAD, *.ts under scripts/ hooks/ lib/ skills/).
  filesReviewed[6]: scripts/eval/run-evals.ts, scripts/eval/tiers/t1-static.ts, scripts/eval/tiers/t2-hermetic.ts, scripts/eval/tiers/t3-judge.ts, skills/loom-canary/rollback-gate.ts, skills/loom-retro/append-guard.ts
